@startuml Order Status Lifecycle Management
!theme plain
title Order Status Lifecycle Management\n(Status Transitions, Automated Jobs, and Event Triggers)

' Participants
actor "Customer" as customer #LightBlue
actor "Admin" as admin #LightGreen
participant "OrderController" as controller #E3F2FD
participant "OrderService" as orderService #E3F2FD
participant "Scheduled Jobs" as scheduler #FFF3E0
participant "TrackingService" as trackingService #E3F2FD
database "Database" as db #E8F5E9
participant "EventSystem" as eventSystem #FCE4EC
participant "Notification\nService" as notificationService #FCE4EC

' ===== INITIAL ORDER CREATION =====
group Status: PENDING_PAYMENT → CONFIRMED
    note over customer, orderService
        **Trigger:** Payment completed
        See Payment Processing diagram
    end note
    
    customer -> controller: Order created with payment_method = 'card'
    controller -> orderService: Order created\n{status: 'pending_payment'}
    
    note over orderService
        Waiting for payment gateway webhook
        Or COD orders confirmed immediately
    end note
    
    alt Payment completed (webhook received)
        controller -> orderService: updateOrderStatus(\n  order_id: 123,\n  new_status: OrderStatus::CONFIRMED,\n  note: 'Payment completed'\n)
        activate orderService
        
        orderService -> db: BEGIN TRANSACTION
        activate db
        
        orderService -> orderService: Validate transition:\nPENDING_PAYMENT → CONFIRMED\nAllowed: ✓
        
        orderService -> db: UPDATE orders\nSET\n  status = 'confirmed',\n  confirmed_at = NOW()\nWHERE id = 123
        
        orderService -> db: INSERT INTO order_status_history\n(\n  order_id: 123,\n  from_status: 'pending_payment',\n  to_status: 'confirmed',\n  changed_by_type: 'system',\n  note: 'Payment completed'\n)
        
        orderService -> db: COMMIT
        deactivate db
        
        orderService -> eventSystem: dispatch('order.confirmed', order)
        activate eventSystem
        eventSystem ->> notificationService: Send order confirmation
        deactivate eventSystem
        
        orderService --> controller: Order updated
        deactivate orderService
        
    else Payment timeout (48 hours)
        note over scheduler
            **Scheduled Job:**
            CancelExpiredOrders.php
            Runs: Every hour
        end note
        
        scheduler -> orderService: Auto-cancel expired orders
        activate orderService
        
        orderService -> db: SELECT * FROM orders\nWHERE status = 'pending_payment'\nAND created_at < NOW() - INTERVAL 48 HOUR
        db --> orderService: Expired orders [3 orders]
        
        loop For each expired order
            orderService -> orderService: cancelOrder(\n  order_id,\n  cancelled_by_type: 'system',\n  reason: 'Payment timeout'\n)
            note right
                See Cancellation diagram
                - Stock restored
                - Status = 'cancelled'
            end note
        end
        
        orderService --> scheduler: 3 orders cancelled
        deactivate orderService
    end
end

' ===== CONFIRMED TO PROCESSING =====
group Status: CONFIRMED → PROCESSING
    note over admin, orderService
        **Trigger:** Admin/system starts order preparation
    end note
    
    admin -> controller: PUT /api/v1/admin/orders/{id}/status\n{status: 'processing'}
    activate controller
    
    controller -> orderService: updateOrderStatus(\n  order_id: 123,\n  new_status: OrderStatus::PROCESSING,\n  changed_by: admin\n)
    activate orderService
    
    orderService -> db: SELECT * FROM orders WHERE id = 123
    db --> orderService: Order {status: 'confirmed'}
    
    orderService -> orderService: Validate transition:\nCONFIRMED → PROCESSING\nAllowed: ✓
    
    alt Transition valid
        orderService -> db: BEGIN TRANSACTION
        activate db
        
        orderService -> db: UPDATE orders\nSET\n  status = 'processing',\n  processing_at = NOW()\nWHERE id = 123
        
        orderService -> db: INSERT INTO order_status_history\n(\n  order_id: 123,\n  from_status: 'confirmed',\n  to_status: 'processing',\n  changed_by_type: 'admin',\n  changed_by: admin.id,\n  note: 'Order preparation started'\n)
        
        orderService -> db: COMMIT
        deactivate db
        
        orderService -> eventSystem: dispatch('order.processing', order)
        activate eventSystem
        eventSystem ->> notificationService: Send processing notification
        deactivate eventSystem
        
        orderService --> controller: Status updated
        deactivate orderService
        
        controller --> admin: ResponseProtocol::success(\n  order,\n  'Order marked as processing'\n)
        deactivate controller
        
    else Invalid transition
        orderService --> controller: ValidationError
        deactivate orderService
        
        controller --> admin: ResponseProtocol::error(\n  {allowed_transitions: [...]},\n  'Invalid status transition',\n  422\n)
        deactivate controller
    end
end

' ===== PROCESSING TO SHIPPED =====
group Status: PROCESSING → SHIPPED
    note over admin, orderService
        **Trigger:** Order dispatched with tracking
    end note
    
    admin -> controller: PUT /api/v1/admin/orders/{id}/ship\n{\n  tracking_number: 'TRK123456789',\n  carrier: 'FedEx',\n  estimated_delivery: '2025-01-05'\n}
    activate controller
    
    controller -> orderService: shipOrder(\n  order_id: 123,\n  tracking_number,\n  carrier,\n  admin\n)
    activate orderService
    
    orderService -> db: BEGIN TRANSACTION
    activate db
    
    orderService -> db: UPDATE orders\nSET\n  status = 'shipped',\n  tracking_number = 'TRK123456789',\n  carrier = 'FedEx',\n  shipped_at = NOW()\nWHERE id = 123
    
    orderService -> db: INSERT INTO order_status_history\n(\n  order_id: 123,\n  from_status: 'processing',\n  to_status: 'shipped',\n  changed_by_type: 'admin',\n  changed_by: admin.id,\n  note: 'Shipped via FedEx - TRK123456789'\n)
    
    alt COD order
        orderService -> db: UPDATE orders\nSET payment_status = 'cod_pending'\nWHERE id = 123
        note right
            Payment collected on delivery
        end note
    end
    
    orderService -> db: COMMIT
    deactivate db
    
    orderService -> eventSystem: dispatch('order.shipped',\n{order, tracking_number, carrier})
    activate eventSystem
    eventSystem ->> notificationService: Send shipping notification\nwith tracking link
    deactivate eventSystem
    
    orderService --> controller: Order shipped
    deactivate orderService
    
    controller --> admin: ResponseProtocol::success(\n  order,\n  'Order marked as shipped'\n)
    deactivate controller
    
    ' Customer tracking
    customer -> controller: GET /api/v1/orders/{orderNumber}/track
    activate controller
    
    controller -> trackingService: getTrackingInfo('TRK123456789', 'FedEx')
    activate trackingService
    
    trackingService -> trackingService: Query carrier API\n(optional integration)
    
    trackingService --> controller: TrackingInfo:\n{\n  status: 'in_transit',\n  location: 'Memphis, TN',\n  estimated_delivery: '2025-01-05',\n  history: [...]\n}
    deactivate trackingService
    
    controller --> customer: ResponseProtocol::success(\n  {order, tracking_info}\n)
    deactivate controller
end

' ===== SHIPPED TO DELIVERED =====
group Status: SHIPPED → DELIVERED
    note over trackingService, orderService
        **Trigger Options:**
        1. Carrier webhook (automated)
        2. Admin manual update
        3. Customer confirmation
    end note
    
    alt Option 1: Carrier Webhook (Automated)
        trackingService ->> controller: POST /api/webhooks/carrier/fedex\n{\n  "tracking_number": "TRK123456789",\n  "status": "delivered",\n  "delivered_at": "2025-01-05 14:30:00",\n  "signature": "John Doe"\n}
        activate controller
        
        controller -> orderService: markDelivered(\n  tracking_number: 'TRK123456789',\n  delivered_at,\n  signature\n)
        activate orderService
        
    else Option 2: Admin Manual Update
        admin -> controller: PUT /api/v1/admin/orders/{id}/deliver
        activate controller
        
        controller -> orderService: markDelivered(order_id, admin)
        activate orderService
        
    else Option 3: Customer Confirmation
        customer -> controller: POST /api/v1/orders/{id}/confirm-delivery
        activate controller
        
        controller -> orderService: markDelivered(order_id, customer)
        activate orderService
    end
    
    orderService -> db: BEGIN TRANSACTION
    activate db
    
    orderService -> db: UPDATE orders\nSET\n  status = 'delivered',\n  delivered_at = NOW()\nWHERE id = 123
    
    orderService -> db: INSERT INTO order_status_history\n(\n  order_id: 123,\n  from_status: 'shipped',\n  to_status: 'delivered',\n  changed_by_type: 'system', // or 'admin' or 'customer'\n  note: 'Package delivered'\n)
    
    alt COD order
        orderService -> db: UPDATE orders\nSET payment_status = 'paid'\nWHERE id = 123
        
        orderService -> db: UPDATE payments\nSET status = 'paid',\npaid_at = NOW()\nWHERE order_id = 123
        
        note right
            **COD Payment Confirmation:**
            Payment collected at delivery
            Update payment status to 'paid'
        end note
    end
    
    orderService -> db: COMMIT
    deactivate db
    
    orderService -> eventSystem: dispatch('order.delivered', order)
    activate eventSystem
    eventSystem ->> notificationService: Send delivery confirmation
    eventSystem ->> scheduler: Schedule auto-complete job\n(7 days from now)
    deactivate eventSystem
    
    orderService --> controller: Order delivered
    deactivate orderService
    
    controller --> customer: ResponseProtocol::success(\n  order,\n  'Order delivered successfully'\n)
    deactivate controller
end

' ===== DELIVERED TO COMPLETED =====
group Status: DELIVERED → COMPLETED
    note over scheduler, orderService
        **Auto-Complete Job:**
        CompleteDeliveredOrders.php
        Runs: Daily at midnight
        
        Logic: Mark orders as completed
        7 days after delivery
    end note
    
    scheduler -> orderService: Auto-complete delivered orders
    activate orderService
    
    orderService -> db: SELECT * FROM orders\nWHERE status = 'delivered'\nAND delivered_at < NOW() - INTERVAL 7 DAY
    db --> orderService: Eligible orders [5 orders]
    
    loop For each order
        orderService -> db: BEGIN TRANSACTION
        activate db
        
        orderService -> db: UPDATE orders\nSET\n  status = 'completed',\n  completed_at = NOW()\nWHERE id = ?
        
        orderService -> db: INSERT INTO order_status_history\n(\n  order_id,\n  from_status: 'delivered',\n  to_status: 'completed',\n  changed_by_type: 'system',\n  note: 'Auto-completed after 7 days'\n)
        
        orderService -> db: COMMIT
        deactivate db
        
        orderService -> eventSystem: dispatch('order.completed', order)
        activate eventSystem
        note over eventSystem
            **Completion Triggers:**
            - Request product review
            - Unlock loyalty points
            - Close support tickets
            - Archive order data
        end note
        eventSystem ->> notificationService: Send review request
        deactivate eventSystem
    end
    
    orderService --> scheduler: 5 orders completed
    deactivate orderService
    
    note over customer
        **Customer receives:**
        - Review request email
        - Loyalty points credited
        - Order marked as completed
    end note
end

' ===== STATUS VALIDATION =====
group Status Transition Validation
    note over orderService
        **Status State Machine:**
        Enforced in OrderStatus enum
        
        canTransitionTo(OrderStatus $to): bool
    end note
    
    orderService -> orderService: Check allowed transitions
    
    note right of orderService
        **Allowed Transitions:**
        
        pending_payment →
          ✓ confirmed
          ✓ cancelled
        
        confirmed →
          ✓ processing
          ✓ cancelled
        
        processing →
          ✓ shipped
          ✓ cancelled
        
        shipped →
          ✓ delivered
          ✗ cannot cancel (use return)
        
        delivered →
          ✓ completed
          ✓ returned
        
        completed →
          ✗ final state (immutable)
        
        cancelled →
          ✗ final state (immutable)
        
        returned →
          ✗ final state (immutable)
    end note
end

' ===== SCHEDULED JOBS =====
group Scheduled Jobs Overview
    note over scheduler
        **1. CancelExpiredOrders.php**
        Schedule: Every hour
        Action: Cancel orders pending payment > 48h
        
        **2. SendPaymentReminders.php**
        Schedule: Daily at 9 AM
        Reminders: 24h, 36h, 48h after order creation
        
        **3. CompleteDeliveredOrders.php**
        Schedule: Daily at midnight
        Action: Mark delivered orders as completed after 7 days
        
        **4. CleanupExpiredCarts.php**
        Schedule: Daily at 2 AM
        Action: Delete expired guest carts (> 30 days old)
    end note
end

' Notes
note over orderService, eventSystem
    **Event-Driven Notifications:**
    
    Each status change dispatches an event:
    
    📧 order.confirmed
       → Email: Order confirmation
       → SMS: Order number
    
    ⚙️ order.processing
       → Email: Preparation started
       → Admin: Dashboard update
    
    📦 order.shipped
       → Email: Shipping notification + tracking
       → SMS: Tracking number
       → Push: Shipment on the way
    
    🏠 order.delivered
       → Email: Delivery confirmation
       → SMS: Package delivered
       → Schedule: Auto-complete in 7 days
    
    ✅ order.completed
       → Email: Review request
       → Loyalty: Credit points
       → Analytics: Track completion rate
    
    ❌ order.cancelled
       → Email: Cancellation confirmation
       → Refund: Process refund
       → Stock: Restore inventory
    
    🔄 order.returned
       → Email: Return confirmation
       → Refund: Process refund
       → QC: Quality check required
end note

note over admin, customer
    **Status Lifecycle Timeline:**
    
    Day 0:  ⏺ pending_payment (Order created)
            ↓ (Payment completed or COD)
    Day 0:  ✓ confirmed (Payment verified)
            ↓ (Admin starts preparation)
    Day 1:  ⚙️ processing (Picking & packing)
            ↓ (Admin dispatches)
    Day 2:  📦 shipped (In transit)
            ↓ (Carrier delivers)
    Day 5:  🏠 delivered (Package received)
            ↓ (Auto after 7 days)
    Day 12: ✅ completed (Final state)
    
    **Alternative Paths:**
    
    Any early status → ❌ cancelled
    delivered → 🔄 returned (customer request)
    
    **Average Timeline:**
    - Standard shipping: ~10 days
    - Express shipping: ~5 days
    - Same-day delivery: < 24 hours
end note

note over db
    **order_status_history Table:**
    
    Provides complete audit trail:
    - Who changed status (customer/admin/system)
    - When changed (timestamp)
    - From/to status (transition)
    - Notes (reason, details)
    
    **Query Examples:**
    
    1. Order timeline:
       SELECT * FROM order_status_history
       WHERE order_id = 123
       ORDER BY created_at
    
    2. Average processing time:
       SELECT AVG(TIMESTAMPDIFF(
         HOUR, confirmed_at, shipped_at
       )) FROM orders
    
    3. Status distribution:
       SELECT status, COUNT(*)
       FROM orders
       GROUP BY status
end note

@enduml
